<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom yr net profit falls to NZ$581 mln.</title>
<headline>Telecom yr net profit falls to NZ$581 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year result to March 31.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   581.4 vs 716.8</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			   10.5 vs 9.5</p>
<p>    Total div for yr (cents)	  39.0 vs 35.0</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   30.8 vs 37.9</p>
<p>    Turnover (bln)			3.10 vs 2.94</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			980.5 vs 1,122.4</p>
<p>    Tax				    311.3 vs 376.0</p>
<p>    Abnormals			    151.5 vs nil</p>
<p>    Pacific Star loss		   50.2 vs 29.6 loss</p>
<p>    Pacific Star provision	    37.4 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (billion)    1.89 vs same</p>
<p>Dividend pay date June 18 in NZ and Australia, June 15 in U.S.</p>
<p>Note - Market expectations were for a net profit of $718 million excluding provisions. Telecom Corp of New Zealand Ltd is a telephone utility 24.9 percent owned by Ameritech Corp and 24.9 pct by Bell Atlantic Corp.</p>
<p>Balance sheet (in billions unless stated)</p>
<p>    Current assets			  0.761 vs 0.738</p>
<p>    Total assets			     4.62 vs 4.49</p>
<p>    Current liabilities		    1.61 vs 1.02</p>
<p>    Total liabilities			2.98 vs 2.34</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		   1.64 vs 2.15</p>
<p>Cashflow from operating activities 1.41 vs 1.23</p>
<p>Cashflow from investing activities(0.670)vs (0.518)</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
